# source: SYNTHETIC
# title: Stray BYE (other Call-ID) changes nothing; a BYE retransmitted after the call ended is still answered 200 and ends nothing
# verdict: DIFFERS
# basis: README: a BYE is acted on only when its Call-ID is the live call's
# reason: cosmetic: a stray BYE (another Call-ID) is answered by gate-sip with the LIVE call's To tag, by Portico with a fresh tag. The behaviours (200, nothing ended) are identical

>>> send
INVITE sip:9901@{{SRV}} SIP/2.0
Via: SIP/2.0/UDP {{ST}};branch=z9hG4bKinv1
From: <sip:8001@{{ST}}>;tag=st-call-1
To: <sip:9901@{{SRV}}>
Call-ID: call-1
CSeq: 1 INVITE
Contact: <sip:8001@{{ST}}>
Content-Type: application/sdp
Max-Forwards: 70

v=0
o=- 0 0 IN IP4 {{STIP}}
s=-
c=IN IP4 {{STIP}}
t=0 0
m=audio {{RTP}} RTP/AVP 97 8 0 18 9 102 103 101
a=rtpmap:97 PCM/16000
a=rtpmap:8 PCMA/8000
a=rtpmap:0 PCMU/8000
a=rtpmap:18 G729/8000
a=rtpmap:9 G722/8000
a=rtpmap:102 G722/16000
a=rtpmap:103 PCM/8000
a=rtpmap:101 telephone-event/8000
m=video 20000 RTP/AVP 96
a=rtpmap:96 H264/90000
.
>>> recv
>>> answer
>>> recv
>>> send
BYE sip:9901@{{SRV}} SIP/2.0
Via: SIP/2.0/UDP {{ST}};branch=z9hG4bKbye1
From: <sip:8001@{{ST}}>;tag=st-some-old-call
To: <sip:9901@{{SRV}}>
Call-ID: some-old-call
CSeq: 2 BYE
Max-Forwards: 70
.
>>> recv
>>> state
>>> send
